<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Rationalising a monomial surd denominator and simplifying into the form k*sqrt(m)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Rationalise the denominator and simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: For example, write <code>9*sqrt(11)</code> to represent \(9\sqrt{11}\).)</i></p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ \frac{{@p@}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@n@}}} \]</p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Multiply the numerator and denominator by \(\sqrt{{@n@}}\)</b><br>
Multiplying top and bottom by \(\sqrt{{@n@}}\) removes the square root from the denominator without changing the value of the fraction:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@n@}}} \times \frac{\sqrt{{@n@}}}{\sqrt{{@n@}}} = \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@n@}}}{{@q@} \times \sqrt{{@n@}} \times \sqrt{{@n@}}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Simplify the denominator</b><br>
Since \(\sqrt{{@n@}} \times \sqrt{{@n@}} = {@n@}\), multiply \({@q@} \times {@n@}\) in the denominator:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@n@}}}{{@q@} \times {@n@}} = \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@n@}}}{{@qn@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Divide the outside numbers to simplify the fraction</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@p@} \div {@qn@} = {@k@} \quad \Longrightarrow \quad \frac{{@p@}\sqrt{{@n@}}}{{@qn@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@p@}}{{@q@}\sqrt{{@n@}}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
